From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:16:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: storage images and texel buffers in software
 shaders

Image loads, stores and atomics read and write the texel in emulated memory where the texture
header says it is (pitch or block linear, the view's level and layer), formatted (converted
from and to the image's format) or typed (the bytes as they are). Texel buffers are fetched the
same way. Textures a shader may have written to are checked again afterwards, fragment and
vertex shaders' writes included.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7DVAudgDzMpBqJZHAz
